 "deviations_from_plan": [
  "Population (decision 2026-10-23): the pipeline registered every .ipynb as a Python notebook (src/repo.sh) and ran it with a Python kernel. --notebook-languages gives each original notebook's kernel language (read from its metadata, analysis/paper/notebook_languages.py); notebooks of other languages are removed, as the plan defines Y_r over Python notebooks, and a resource left without a Python notebook is ineligible (no replacement: domain estimation). Notebooks without language metadata stay in, as before.",
  "S3: the \"archived\" covariate is not recorded for all platforms (no Zenodo equivalent); it is left out.",
  "S1: the mixed model is fitted unweighted (variational Bayes, statsmodels BinomialBayesMixedGLM); the design-based platform estimates are the primary ones.",
  "S3/RQ4: the pooled fractional logit uses Zenodo weights normalised to mean 1 within the platform, so each platform contributes its sample size; it describes associations in the sample, not population effects.",
  "S4: chi-square tests use notebook counts and ignore the clustering in resources (descriptive only).",
  "Section 7: resources whose results were damaged by the infrastructure or the pipeline, not by the resource, are listed in --infrastructure, excluded from the primary analysis and included as recorded in sensitivity 8. Round 1 (decision 2026-10-11): 8 resources hit by the full node-local /tmp (infrastructure-failures.csv). Round 2 (decision 2026-10-20): 8 resources (infrastructure-failures-r2.csv): 5 hit by a full node-local /tmp during the run, 1 whose output comparison failed (pipeline Python could not import attrs), 2 pipeline path bugs.",
  "Y_r: Python notebooks of an analysable resource without an execution record count as not clean (sensitivity: excluded)."
 ],
